.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt LOONGARCH_TIMER 4 loongarch64
.Os
.\" .Nm loongarch64/loongarch_timer
.\" .Nm loongarch64/timer
.Sh NAME
.Nm loongarch_timer ,
.Nm timer
.Nd LoongArch CPU timer and timecounter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
This driver is a standard part of the LoongArch kernel and attaches as
.Dv timer0 .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a timecounter based on the stable CPU counter and a
per-CPU event timer supporting periodic and one-shot operation.
The timer interrupt is delivered through
.Xr cpuic 4 .
.Pp
The counter frequency is derived from the base frequency, multiplier,
and divisor reported by CPUCFG registers.
The CPU must advertise the stable counter and timer feature and provide
nonzero frequency parameters.
.Pp
No driver-specific kernel configuration directive is required.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "timer0: No clock frequency specified"
The CPU does not advertise the required timer feature or supplies
invalid frequency parameters.
.It "timer0: Unable to alloc int resource."
The driver could not register its CPU-local timer interrupt handler.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpuic 4 ,
.Xr eventtimers 4 ,
.Xr timecounters 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver was added in the LoongArch port of
.Fx 16.0 .
